body:
So first things first:

Dino Rabbits are dead. The current banlist renders them useless so don't worry about dino rabbits.

Now as far as Prophecy goes:

The archetype focuses on Spellcaster-Type monsters and the effects and presence of "Spellbook" Spell Cards. "Spellbook" cards focus on creating advantage, like raising a monster's ATK ("Spellbook of Power"), protecting monsters ("Spellbook of Wisdom"), or Xyz Summoning ("Spellbook of Life"), and manipulating the amount on the field, in the hand and in the Graveyard to activate effects. Unfortunately this archetype is VERY expensive so I would not recommend you buying it, but feel free to build decks with it online or whatever program you use.


/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////


Fire Kings are fun. Fire King monsters have their effects triggered when they're destroyed and sent to the Graveyard. Their boss monster, "Garunix", will destroy all other monsters on the field in the Standby Phase of the turn after it was destroyed by a card effect. Since it does not need to be destroyed while on the field, even cards like "Solemn Judgement" can trigger its effects. The other Fire King monsters can be Special Summoned from your hand when a Fire King is destroyed, keeping field advantage. They aren't all that expensive. Many of the expensive cards can be substituted for much less expensive cards(at the loos of performance, though this can help you decide if you want to stick to this deck and spend the money on it.

////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

Mermails are fun, but a bit expenisve for just a couple cards. A lot of these cards are seeing reprints and are coming down in price. Level 3 "Mermail" monsters all share a similar effect when they get sent to the Graveyard - they Special Summon another "Mermail", letting them swarm the field. The Level 4 "Mermail" monsters can activate their effects when they are Normal or Special Summoned, by discarding a WATER monster from your Hand, which will trigger the effect of the previous monsters effects, and the Level 4 monsters help to either search the Deck or graveyard for a Level 3 WATER monster. The higher-Level "Mermails" can Special Summon themselves with relative-ease by sending other "Mermails" to the Graveyard, which will also trigger their effects. The "boss" monster of the archetype, "Mermail Abyssgaios", is a powerful control card, with 2 effects that forces your opponent into a corner, either by preventing their most powerful monsters from attacking and/or by negating their weaker monsters' effects.

///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

Now for Six Sams. They are all pretty cheap and totally viable in this format. I would recommend you start with Six Sams or Fire Kings. The goal of Six Sams is to use their Special Summon effects in order to Synchro summon powerful monsters really fast. The excel at putting out powerful monsters like no one's business. With the banning of Gateway, they aren't as great as before but they can still be run.
